{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV","text":"KComponents","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P12ConnectivityE11kComponentsAD11KComponentsVyxGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:11Hypergraphs18IncidenceGraphViewV","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Hypergraphs"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"kComponents()","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Connectivity\/KComponents.swift#L80","fileName":"KComponents.swift"}},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview\/kcomponents()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/KComponents","text":"KComponents","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/kComponents()"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Inherited from ","type":"text"},{"code":"Graph.kComponents()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs":{"title":"Hypergraphs","abstract":[],"type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/IncidenceGraphView/kComponents()":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview\/kcomponents()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/kComponents()","title":"kComponents()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV","text":"KComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/KComponents":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/kcomponents","title":"KComponents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-components of an undirected graph (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k ≥ 1,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the maximal sets of vertices whose induced subgraph is k-vertex-connected, that is, has more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than k vertices and stays connected after removing any k − 1 of them. The 1-components are the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connected components with an edge, the 2-components the blocks of three or more vertices; every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"k-component lies inside a (k − 1)-component. Components at one level may share fewer than k"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/KComponents","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"KComponents","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/IncidenceGraphView":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a "},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"0 ..< n + m","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"code":"i < n","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex index "},{"code":"i","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is hyperedge "},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with an edge "},{"code":"{i, n + p}","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for each incidence. It is bipartite and simple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(vertices on the left, hyperedges on the right), an empty hyperedge is an isolated vertex, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it loses nothing."}],"title":"IncidenceGraphView","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview"}}}